defmodule <%= module %>.Docs do
  @moduledoc """
  <%= module %>'s Docs domain — the samen_core Docs scope blueprint (ADR-004; F3)
  mounted AS-IS, exactly as samenerp (`Samenerp.Docs`), driftwood
  (`Driftwood.Docs`) and pawchart (`PawChart.Docs`) mount it, plus the WS-Notes
  block model (ADR-053 §3, M1).

  One `use` expands into the FOUR host-owned resources — the internal-document
  substrate this app inherits at ≈0 authored LOC:

    * `<%= module %>.Docs.Doc` — a titled page (`<%= d_doc %>`): `title`, `body`
      (plain, `Samen.Pii.FreeTextScan`-guarded) / 🔒 `secure_body`
      (`vault: :pii_doc_body`), the generic `(subject_key, subject_id)` object-ref
      anchor, and the ADR-053 page-tree columns `parent_doc_id` (same-org —
      `Samen.Policy.SameOrgFk`), `icon`, `position` and `revision`. Archivable.
    * `<%= module %>.Docs.Note` — the untitled annotation (`<%= d_note %>`), same
      anchor, same pair (`vault: :pii_note_body`). Archivable.
    * `<%= module %>.Docs.DocBlock` — one typed BLOCK row of a page
      (`<%= d_block %>`): `type` is a bounded enum whose `metadata`/`checked` are
      validated against it by `Samen.Scopes.Docs.BlockShape` on the governed write
      path, `position` is an integer ordinal scoped to its parent, and
      🔒 `text_secure` (`vault: :pii_block_text`) is the vaulted half of the
      per-block `text`/`text_secure` pair — masking granularity at the COLUMN
      level, where `pii_classify`/`no_plaintext_pii`/`pii_reads` already look.
      Archivable.
    * `<%= module %>.Docs.DocLink` — one RESOLVED `[[Title]]` edge
      (`<%= d_link %>`); both endpoints same-org, so a backlink is an indexed
      reverse query and a title in another org never resolves. Not archivable — a
      pure edge row.

  ## Abbrevs

  `<%= d_doc %>`/`<%= d_note %>`/`<%= d_block %>`/`<%= d_link %>` are prefix-derived
  and reserved in the GLOBAL registry (samen_core/priv/abbrev_registry.json) by
  `mix samen.gen.app` when it emits this app — never hand-edited (ADR-023).

  ## What is deliberately NOT here

  No routes, no LiveView and no nav label: the pages SURFACE is WS-Notes Phase 3.
  This mount is the model half — rows, classification and the masking seam — so a
  host that mounts it gains the substrate and its verifier posture without a UI.
  """
  use Ash.Domain, validate_config_inclusion?: false

  use Samen.Scopes.Docs,
    otp_app: :<%= otp_app %>,
    repo: <%= module %>.Repo,
    namespace: <%= module %>.Docs,
    abbrevs: %{
      doc: "<%= d_doc %>",
      note: "<%= d_note %>",
      doc_block: "<%= d_block %>",
      doc_link: "<%= d_link %>"
    }
end
